WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.420 --> 00:00:12.659
So I'm going to talk to you today about

00:00:13.330 --> 00:00:15.330
a different way of looking at

00:00:15.699 --> 00:00:17.470
what real is.

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:21.449
It's not easy to figure out what real is because we don't really have infinite knowledge

00:00:21.449 --> 00:00:25.559
and so we're always making some sets of presuppositions about what's most real

00:00:26.230 --> 00:00:28.090
And it really matters what

00:00:28.090 --> 00:00:30.070
you assume is most real because

00:00:30.070 --> 00:00:36.930
you base the decisions that you make that run the entire course of your life on those assumptions whether you recognize it or not,

00:00:37.240 --> 00:00:39.240
and if you get the assumptions wrong

00:00:40.020 --> 00:00:45.380
or even if you leave them incomplete, you're going to pay a big price for it

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:47.800
and

00:00:48.160 --> 00:00:50.369
the assumptions that we use in our culture,

00:00:51.250 --> 00:00:56.369
although they've enabled us to develop a tremendously potent technology

00:00:56.600 --> 00:01:00.599
are incomplete in ways that have also cost us, and that are extremely dangerous.

00:01:01.930 --> 00:01:04.589
Since the Scientific Age began,

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.500
we've lived in a universe

00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.430
where

00:01:09.430 --> 00:01:11.260
the bottom

00:01:11.260 --> 00:01:15.599
strata of reality is considered to be something, that's dead

00:01:16.119 --> 00:01:17.140
like

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:19.979
dirt, it's like it's matter, it's

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:22.650
objective, it's

00:01:24.040 --> 00:01:26.040
external and

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:31.739
there isn't any element of it that lends any reality

00:01:32.000 --> 00:01:33.189
to

00:01:33.189 --> 00:01:35.219
phenomena like meaning or purpose.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:40.259
That's all being relegated to the subjective and in some ways to the illusory

00:01:41.320 --> 00:01:42.610
but

00:01:42.610 --> 00:01:47.519
It's by no means self-evident that that set of presuppositions is correct,

00:01:48.520 --> 00:01:50.520
because we lack

00:01:51.070 --> 00:01:56.430
Infinite knowledge, and there's many things about the structure of being that we don't understand, the main one being

00:01:56.500 --> 00:02:04.349
consciousness, we can't account for it at all and we can't account for the role it appears to play in the transformation of potential into

00:02:04.350 --> 00:02:05.320
actuality

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:10.440
which is a role that's been recognized by physicists for almost a hundred years now

00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:11.590
and

00:02:11.590 --> 00:02:14.500
which remains one of the biggest unsolved mystery in science.

00:02:15.700 --> 00:02:18.180
There are other ways of looking at what's real

00:02:18.800 --> 00:02:21.820
And these other ways have some advantages and one of the advantages that

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:25.140
they have is that they protect us knowing these other ways of

00:02:25.610 --> 00:02:30.849
operating within reality defining reality protect us from certain kinds of Pathologies and modern people are prone to

00:02:31.400 --> 00:02:36.400
a fair number of pathologies that stem from the assumptions of their,

00:02:36.739 --> 00:02:44.378
of the systems they use to define reality and one of those pathologies is a kind of a nihilistic hopelessness which is a

00:02:44.510 --> 00:02:46.510
consequence of the recognition that,

00:02:46.549 --> 00:02:50.229
in the final analysis nothing really has any meaning

00:02:50.800 --> 00:02:54.369
And because life is difficult, and that's a meaning that you can't escape

00:02:56.120 --> 00:03:02.079
Being forced to abandon your belief in a positive or a transcendent meaning can leave you weak the times when you really

00:03:02.389 --> 00:03:04.389
can least afford to be weak

00:03:04.400 --> 00:03:10.509
And there's more important pathologies that it's opened us up to too and those are pathologies of belief, and I think we saw the most

00:03:11.389 --> 00:03:19.179
Horrifying examples of that hopefully the most horrifying examples in the 20th century where people whose belief systems were shattered at least in part

00:03:19.180 --> 00:03:24.220
by the competition between religious and scientific Viewpoints turned in large numbers

00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:31.780
to mass movements that were in error in every way as substitute ,a more rational in some sense substitute for

00:03:32.389 --> 00:03:37.749
Religious beliefs that appeared no longer tenable and the consequence of that was it was just about annihilation

00:03:38.780 --> 00:03:46.299
Because we came close to annihilation twice once in the 60s and once in the 80s and even without the totality of annihilation

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.959
we lost hundreds of millions of people as a consequence

00:03:50.540 --> 00:03:54.400
of pathological belief systems in the 20th century, so

00:03:54.979 --> 00:03:57.009
if belief systems become pathological

00:03:57.500 --> 00:04:05.019
they put that Pathology can pose the biggest threat possibly to our very existence and if you're a Darwinian in any sense

